  "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}2\\,522 & = & 1\\,092(2) & + & 338 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 1\\,092 & = & 338(3) & + & 78 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 338 & = & 78(4) & + & 26 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 78 & = & 26(3) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $26.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $2\\,522$ and $1\\,092$ is $26.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(2\\,522,1\\,092)=26.\n$$",
